# DEPRECATED — use the manual workflow_dispatch button instead.
#
# The official-candidate workflow now supports workflow_dispatch with a
# required "reason" input. To trigger a fresh official candidate build:
#
#   1. Go to Actions → "Official Candidate Build & Publish (Woodbox)"
#   2. Click "Run workflow", select main, enter a reason.
#   3. The build runs and publishes without a PR or noop commit.
#
# The old procedure (touch this file in a PR, merge to main) still
# works mechanically — any push to main triggers the workflow — but
# it creates unnecessary ceremony and clutters the git log. Prefer
# the workflow_dispatch button for all new freshen requests.
